Having ascended a tourist and a wizard, both with little/no divine
protection, I'm interested in changing strategies and attempting a
protection run with a weak gnomish/dwarvish character such as an
archaeologist or healer, preferably archeologist.

I've only sucessfully completed the run twice in X (X > 20) games, and
want to improve the sucess rate, but even writing Elbereth in the dust
and digging pits for defense don't seem to improve my archaeologist's
survivability. The biggest hurdles my arcs have encountered are

1. Minetown
I often end up at minetown via trap door, without my pet. Trying to
keep pacifist conduct w/o a pet is insane. I've attempted to cloister
the monsters by writing Elbereths in the dust in the corridors, but
the monsters don't *seem* to respect E unless I'm standing on it.
Furthermore, if I'm in deep trouble, the Minetown watch seem to clog
corridors needed for escape.

2. Getting enough loot / divine protection (aka 2000 zorkmids and exp
1, for 9 units protection guarantee)
Arcs don't spellcast and can't heal themselves, so surviving long
enough to accumulate 2000 Zorkmids from vaults/gems requires extreme
caution. Pits, E squares, etc. And *no healing* except loafing on dust-
written E-squares in early game.

3. Keeping pet close by
Essential for a protection run, but my pets unfortunately have other
plans, such as attacking floating eyes, blue jellies and watch
captains, investigating rock traps, and wandering off. The Arc's
intrinsic speed doesn't help this.

If anybody here has more sucess with protection runs than I do, feel
free to help.



